{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/916818-did-they-ever-do-dullahan","id":916818,"title":"Did they ever do Dullahan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-18T07:25:48-07:00","id":916818,"title":"Did they ever do Dullahan?","content":"There were so many books, and a couple lines I never really followed, did any of the lines ever stat out (either as a PC option or as a monster) Dullahans (the Irish Headless Horseman Grim Reaper thing)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T07:49:10-07:00","id":916831,"title":"","content":"Not to my knowledge. Though I see them in Wraith: the Oblivion/Orpheus where they could be used in several ways, depending on whether or not they are wraiths or spectres. In the latter it's rather straight forward while the former could be a band of Irish Renegades that have intentionally moliated themselves into the image of the mythical Dullahans to strike fear in the hearts of Legion wraiths. Or vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomita