ng>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/916818-did-they-ever-do-dullahan?p=916846#post916846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In modern media they tend to get depicted as Undead, but in actual Irish legend they were a type of Unseelie Sidhe. So, I could easily see them cropping up in a lot of places. Was there a Changeling supplement that hit Ireland in particular?</div> </div> </div> </div>Court of All Kings, which was fairly early on in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}